Morrow changes-metadata-v1 canonical wire specification
Version: 1

This normative file is ASCII text with LF line endings and a final LF.
The profile digest is SHA256 of every byte of this file, without conversion.
This file does not embed its own digest.
All integers below are unsigned little-endian. There is no padding.

Offset  Size  Field
0       8     Magic: ASCII MRCHG001
8       2     Version: u16, exactly 1
10      32    Profile digest: exact SHA256 of this normative file
42      32    Scope digest: nonzero
74      32    Window ID: nonzero, exactly outer Frame.source_epoch
106     8     Revision: u64, nonzero
114     32    Card SHA256: SHA256 of the complete Card.encode() bytes
146     2     Card ID byte length: u16, 1 through 256 inclusive
148     2     Operation ID byte length: u16, 1 through 256 inclusive
150     N     Card ID: exactly N original UTF-8 bytes
150+N   M     Operation ID: exactly M original UTF-8 bytes

The payload length is exactly 150+N+M, at most 662 bytes.
Identifiers are valid UTF-8 with no Unicode control character, slash,
backslash, or colon. Do not trim, normalize, or substitute their bytes.
Reject unknown versions, wrong profile digests, invalid identifiers,
zero scope/window/revision, short data, excessive lengths, and trailing data.
There are no optional fields. Any extension requires a new explicit contract.
Card SHA256 is the full Card digest, never a digest of body bytes alone.

The scope digest is SHA256 of this exact concatenation:
  ASCII Morrow/changes-metadata/scope/v1 followed by one NUL byte
  profile_digest[32]
  durable_store_id[32]
  consumer_package_digest[32]
  card_count_u32LE
  repeated(sorted_card_byte_length_u16LE || sorted_card_original_UTF8_bytes)
The fixed card set has 1 through 32 distinct valid identifiers inclusive.
Sort by unsigned original UTF-8 bytes. Reject duplicates and zero Store or
consumer package identities. Do not include private operation positions.
The existing durable Store identity is a logical identity only: a database
copy may preserve it. This commitment is not authorization or anti-cloning.

The public cursor is SHA256 of this exact concatenation:
  ASCII Morrow/changes-metadata/cursor/v1 followed by one NUL byte
  complete canonical payload bytes
The cursor is exactly 32 bytes. It is not an operation sequence or grant.
Outer Frame.sequence remains the channel delivery ordinal. Outer frame
hashes, this cursor, and the profile digest have distinct meanings.
The host must check the outer frame epoch and metadata window ID match.

This is a metadata-only, fixed-set, finite-window invalidation profile.
It contains no body, title, preview, attachment, global sequence, hidden
upper bound, scan count, gap count, path, account, grant, or SQL metadata.
A fresh window needs fresh receiver-specific approval. Reopening after a
verified latest ACK creates a new window; it never restores an old grant,
old hidden upper bound, or an unacknowledged private scan position.
